    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00429',',AA.Nen00429,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,king george;revolutionary war,,aPRA1_75 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The king of England during the American Revolution was King George.  What was his number (i.e. 1st  2nd  etc...)?,It was King Gorge III.,Answer=3 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00430',',AA.Nen00430,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,lantern;old north church;bell tower;british,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many lanterns were hung in the Old North Church on 18 May 1775?,A system had been set up whereby an outlook in the bell tower of the Old North Church would hang one lantern to indicate that the British advance was by land over Boston Neck; or two lanterns to indicate that the British advance was by water across the Charles River to Charlestown. From his location in Charlestown; Revere saw the signal; two lanterns that meant the British were rowing across the river.,Answer=2 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00431',',AA.Nen00431,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,AbCiGoNa EvPoMoCi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,,CiUS,north carolina;civil war;bill of rights,,aPRA1_80 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Each state was given a copy of the Bill of Rights. North Carolina~s original copy was stolen during the civil war.  How many years before it was recovered?,Each state was given a copy of the Bill of Rights. North Carolina~s original copy was stolen during the civil war by members of the Union Army. It was recovered 138 years later in March; 2003.,Answer=138 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00432',',AA.Nen00432,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,AbCiGoNa EvPoMoCi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,,CiUS,congress;declaration of independence,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many member of Congress were there when the Declaration of Independence was signed?,On 28 June 1776; Jefferson~s Declaration of Independence is ready and is presented to the Congress; with changes made by Adams and Franklin. On July 2; twelve of thirteen colonial delegations (New York abstains) vote in support of Lee~s resolution for independence. On July 4; the Congress formally endorses Jefferson~s Declaration; with copies to be sent to all of the colonies. The actual signing of the document occurs on August 2; as most of the 55 members of Congress place their names on the parchment copy.,Answer=55 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00433',',AA.Nen00433,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,AbCiGoNa EvPoMoCi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,,CiUS,constitution;monetary threshold;trial by jury;civil case;twenty dollars;common law,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Amendment VII to the Constitution places a monetary  threshold on when a person can demand a trial by jury in a civil case.  What is the threshold in dollars?,Amendment VII: In suits at common law; where the value in controversy shall exceed twenty dollars; the right of trial by jury shall be preserved; and no fact tried by a jury; shall be otherwise reexamined in any court of the United States; than according to the rules of the common law.,Answer=20 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00434',',AA.Nen00434,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,AbCiGoNa EvPoMoCi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,,CiUS,bill of right;amendment;constitution,,aPRA1_80 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The Bill of Rights are Amendments that were added to the U.S. Constitution.  How many of them are there?,The Bill of Rights are the First Ten Amendments that were added to the U.S. Constitution. The amendments were approved or ratified on December 15; 1789. The Bill of Rights protected the Colonists from tyrannical rule like they had experienced during and even before the American Revolution.,Answer=10 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00435',',AA.Nen00435,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,AbCiGoNa EvPoMoCi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,,CiUS,states;ratify;constitution,,aPRA1_80 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many states were required to ratify the Constitution?,The ratification of the conventions of nine states; shall be sufficient for the establishment of this Constitution between the states so ratifying the same.,Answer=9 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00436',',AA.Nen00436,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,AbCiGoNa EvPoMoCi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,,CiUS,article;constitution,,aPRA1_65 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many articles in the Constitution?,,Answer=7 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00437',',AA.Nen00437,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,prisoners of war;revolutionaries;military casualty;american revolutionaries war,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Of the 25 Thousand Americans who died on active service in the Revolu tionary War how many thousand died as a direct result of battle?,An estimated 25;000 American Revolutionaries died during active military service. About 8;000 of these deaths were in battle; the other 17;000 deaths were from disease; including about 8;000 who died while prisoners of war. The number of Revolutionaries seriously wounded or disabled by the war has been estimated from 8;500 to 25;000. The total American military casualty figure was therefore as high as 50;000.[19],Answer=8 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00438',',AA.Nen00438,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,prisoners of war;american revolution;death;battle,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Of the 25 Thousand Americans who died on active service in the American Revolution` how many thousand died while prisoners of war?,An estimated 25;000 American Revolutionaries died during active military service. About 8;000 of these deaths were in battle; the other 17;000 deaths were from disease; including about 8;000 who died while prisoners of war. The number of Revolutionaries seriously wounded or disabled by the war has been estimated from 8;500 to 25;000. The total American military casualty figure was therefore as high as 50;000.[19],Answer=8 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00439',',AA.Nen00439,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,hessian;german mercenaries;christmas;trenton;washington,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,In the Battle of Trenton` Washington took over a thousand prisoners.  How many Americans were wounded?,December 25 26; 1776 - On Christmas; George Washington takes 2400 of his men and recrosses the Delaware River. Washington then conducts a surprise raid on 1500 British-Hessians (German mercenaries) at Trenton; New Jersey. The Hessians surrender after an hour with nearly 1000 taken prisoner by Washington who suffers only six wounded (including future president Lt. James Monroe). Washington reoccupies Trenton. The victory provides a much needed boost to the morale of all American Patriots.,Answer=6 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00440',',AA.Nen00440,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,boston massacre;patriots;snowball;soldier,,aPRA1_85 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many people were killed in the Boston Massacre?,About four hundred men had gathered in front of the Customs House where  eight British sentries were standing guard  A group of Patriots threw snowballs and teased a British sentry.  The British soldiers became upset with the Patriots. Someone shouted "Fire!" and the soldiers shot into the crowd.  Five people were killed.,Answer=5 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00441',',AA.Nen00441,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,yorktown;revolutionary war;reinforcements;chesapeake bay,,aPRA1_85 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When the British surrendered Yorktown` how many days were they away from a force of 7 thousand reinforcement troops arriving to aid them?,On 24 October 1781 - 7000 British reinforcements under General Clinton arrive at Chesapeake Bay but turn back on hearing of the surrender at Yorktown.,Answer=5 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00442',',AA.Nen00442,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,british soldiers;patriots;boston massacre,,aPRA1_80 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Approximately how many hundred people participated in the Boston Massacre?,About four hundred men had gathered in front of the Customs House where  eight British sentries were standing guard  A group of Patriots threw snowballs and teased a British sentry.  The British soldiers became upset with the Patriots. Someone shouted "Fire!" and the soldiers shot into the crowd.  Five people were killed.,Answer=4 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00443',',AA.Nen00443,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,boston harbor;son of liberty;mohawk indians;tea party,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many crates of tea were dumped into Boston Harbor?,About 50 members of the political organization; The Sons of Liberty; boarded 3 ships in Boston Harbor. Some were dressed; not very convincingly; as Mohawk Indians and dumped 342 crates of tea overboard. In a very orderly and quiet fashion; it was valued at  9;659 pounds sterling.,Answer=342 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00444',',AA.Nen00444,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,french soldiers;count de rochambeau;blockade,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Six thousand French soldiers arrived at Newport in July of 1780` but were blocked by the British Fleet from getting out.  How many days were they stuck there?,July 11; 1780 - 6000 French soldiers under Count de Rochambeau arrive at Newport; Rhode Island. They will remain there for nearly a year; blockaded by the British fleet.,Answer=339 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00445',',AA.Nen00445,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle of lexington;battle of concord;lexington;concord;british;american casualties,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,There were 95 American casualties in the Battles of Lexington and Concord.  How many British?,The Battle of Lexington and Concord resulted in 273 total casualties for the British and 95 for the American rebels.,Answer=273 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00446',',AA.Nen00446,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle of lexington;battle of concord;lexington;concord;british;american casualties,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many British casualties in the Battles of Lexington and Concord?,The Battle of Lexington and Concord resulted in 273 total casualties for the British and 95 for the American rebels.,Answer=273 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00447',',AA.Nen00447,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle of saratoga;general horatio gates;benedict arnold;british,,aPRA1_90 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The British lost 600 men in the Battle of Saratoga.  How many did the Americans lose?,On 7 October 7 1777 - The Battle of Saratoga results in the first major American victory of the Revolutionary War as General Horatio Gates and General Benedict Arnold defeat General Burgoyne; inflicting 600 British casualties with American losses at 150.,Answer=150 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00448',',AA.Nen00448,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,naval engagement;british;valcour bay;lake champlain;gunship,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,In a major naval engagement of the war` the British defeated the Americans in the  Battle of Valcour Bay?  Approximately how many gunships were involved?,October 11; 1776 - A big defeat for the inexperienced American Navy on Lake Champlain at the hands of a British fleet of 87 gunships. In the 7 hour Battle of Valcour Bay most of the American flotilla of 83 gunships is crippled with the remaining ships destroyed in a second engagement two days later.,Answer=150 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00449',',AA.Nen00449,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,america loyalists;revolutionary war,,aPRA1_90 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,By the end of April 1783` how many thousand Loyalists had fled America?,April 26; 1783 - 7000 Loyalists set sail from New York for Canada; bringing a total of 100;000 Loyalists who have now fled America.,Answer=100 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00450',',AA.Nen00450,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle lexington;battle concord;lexington;concord;american casualties;british casualties,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,There were 273 British casualties in the Battles of Lexington and Concord.  How many American casualties?,The Battle of Lexington and Concord resulted in 273 total casualties for the British and 95 for the American rebels.,Answer=95 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00451',',AA.Nen00451,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,the white of their eyes;musket volley;bunker hill;breed~s hill;causalities,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The Americans lost 400 when the British succeed in taking Bunker Hill.  How many did the British loose?,On 17 June 1775 - The first major fight between British and American troops occurs at Boston in the Battle of Bunker Hill. American troops are dug in along the high ground of Breed~s Hill (the actual location) and are attacked by a frontal assault of over 2000 British soldiers who storm up the hill. The Americans are ordered not to fire until they can see "the whites of their eyes." As the British get within 15 paces; the Americans let loose a deadly volley of musket fire and halt the British advance. The British then regroup and attack 30 minutes later with the same result. A third attack; however; succeeds as the Americans run out of ammunition and are left only with bayonets and stones to defend themselves. The British succeed in taking the hill; but at a loss of half their force; over a thousand casualties; with the Americans losing about 400; including important colonial leader; General Joseph Warren.,Answer=1000 LowBracket=500 Type=Integer HiBracket=1500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00452',',AA.Nen00452,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,concord;weapon depot;general gage,,aPRA1_85 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many British soldiers were ordered to Concord to destroy the colonists~ weapons depot?,April 18; 1775 - General Gage orders 700 British soldiers to Concord to destroy the colonists~ weapons depot.,Answer=700 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=1000,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00453',',AA.Nen00453,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle saratoga;british;revolutionary war;benedict arnold;general burgoyne,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The Americans lost 150 men in the Battle of Saratoga.  How many did the British lose?,On 7 October 7 1777 - The Battle of Saratoga results in the first major American victory of the Revolutionary War as General Horatio Gates and General Benedict Arnold defeat General Burgoyne; inflicting 600 British casualties with American losses at 150.,Answer=600 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=1000,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00454',',AA.Nen00454,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,canadians;battle of quebec;quebec,,aPRA1_90 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The British and Canadians lost 20 men in the Battle of Quebec.  How many did the American loose?,On 31st December 1775; with the addition of Montgomery?s troops; Arnold launched night attacks at either end of the city in a snowstorm. The garrison alerted by premature feint attacks on other parts of the city perimeter. Montgomery?s assault was repelled with heavy grapeshot and Montgomery was killed. Arnold?s attack penetrated the city wall but he was wounded. Maclean arrived from dealing with Montgomery?s assault and led the counter attack. The American troops who had penetrated the walls were captured and the assault was driven off. casualties: British and Canadian losses were 20. The American losses were around 500.,Answer=500 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=1000,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00455',',AA.Nen00455,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,bunker hill;breed~s hill,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The British succeed in taking Bunker Hill` but at a loss of half their force with over a thousand casualties.  How many did the Americans loose?,On 17 June 1775 - The first major fight between British and American troops occurs at Boston in the Battle of Bunker Hill. American troops are dug in along the high ground of Breed~s Hill (the actual location) and are attacked by a frontal assault of over 2000 British soldiers who storm up the hill. The Americans are ordered not to fire until they can see "the whites of their eyes." As the British get within 15 paces; the Americans let loose a deadly volley of musket fire and halt the British advance. The British then regroup and attack 30 minutes later with the same result. A third attack; however; succeeds as the Americans run out of ammunition and are left only with bayonets and stones to defend themselves. The British succeed in taking the hill; but at a loss of half their force; over a thousand casualties; with the Americans losing about 400; including important colonial leader; General Joseph Warren.,Answer=400 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00456',',AA.Nen00456,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,french soldiers;newport rhodes island;british fleet;blockaded,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,In July of 1780` a force of French Soldiers arrived at Newport Rhodes Island but were blocked by the British Fleet from getting out. How many thousand French Soldiers were there?,July 11; 1780 - 6000 French soldiers under Count de Rochambeau arrive at Newport; Rhode Island. They will remain there for nearly a year; blockaded by the British fleet.,Answer=6 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=10,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00457',',AA.Nen00457,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,british soldiers;bunker hill;breed~s hill;the whites og their eyes,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Approximately how many thousand British soldiers stormed  Bunker Hill?,On 17 June 1775 - The first major fight between British and American troops occurs at Boston in the Battle of Bunker Hill. American troops are dug in along the high ground of Breed~s Hill (the actual location) and are attacked by a frontal assault of over 2000 British soldiers who storm up the hill. The Americans are ordered not to fire until they can see "the whites of their eyes." As the British get within 15 paces; the Americans let loose a deadly volley of musket fire and halt the British advance. The British then regroup and attack 30 minutes later with the same result. A third attack; however; succeeds as the Americans run out of ammunition and are left only with bayonets and stones to defend themselves. The British succeed in taking the hill; but at a loss of half their force; over a thousand casualties; with the Americans losing about 400; including important colonial leader; General Joseph Warren.,Answer=2 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=10,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00458',',AA.Nen00458,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,fishing creek;south carolina;charles cornwallis;american defeat,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The battle of Fishing Creek` South Carolina was a major defeat for the Americans.  How many hundred Americas were killed or captured?,On 16 August 1780 there was a big defeat for the Americans  at Fishing Creek; South Carolina as forces under General Gates are defeated by troops of General Charles Cornwallis; resulting in 900 Americans killed and 1000 captured.,Answer=19 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=50,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00459',',AA.Nen00459,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,trenton;christmas;washington;delaware river;hessians;james monroe,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,In the Battle of Trenton` only six Americans were wounded.  How many of the enemy were taken prisoner?,December 25 26; 1776 - On Christmas; George Washington takes 2400 of his men and recrosses the Delaware River. Washington then conducts a surprise raid on 1500 British-Hessians (German mercenaries) at Trenton; New Jersey. The Hessians surrender after an hour with nearly 1000 taken prisoner by Washington who suffers only six wounded (including future president Lt. James Monroe). Washington reoccupies Trenton. The victory provides a much needed boost to the morale of all American Patriots.,Answer=1000 LowBracket=500 Type=Integer HiBracket=1500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00460',',AA.Nen00460,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,the white of their eyes;musket volley;bunker hill;breed~s hill;causalities,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Of the 2 thousand British soldiers who storm up Bunker Hill` how many become causalities?,On 17 June 1775 - The first major fight between British and American troops occurs at Boston in the Battle of Bunker Hill. American troops are dug in along the high ground of Breed~s Hill (the actual location) and are attacked by a frontal assault of over 2000 British soldiers who storm up the hill. The Americans are ordered not to fire until they can see "the whites of their eyes." As the British get within 15 paces; the Americans let loose a deadly volley of musket fire and halt the British advance. The British then regroup and attack 30 minutes later with the same result. A third attack; however; succeeds as the Americans run out of ammunition and are left only with bayonets and stones to defend themselves. The British succeed in taking the hill; but at a loss of half their force; over a thousand casualties; with the Americans losing about 400; including important colonial leader; General Joseph Warren.,Answer=1000 LowBracket=500 Type=Integer HiBracket=1500,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00461',',AA.Nen00461,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,lafayette;marqui de lafayette;major general;revolutionary war;philadelphia;volunteer;congress;continental army;aides,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How old was the Marquis de Lafayette when he became a Major General?,On 27 July 27 1777 - Marquis de Lafayette; a 19 year old French aristocrat; arrives in Philadelphia and volunteers to serve without pay. Congress appoints him as a major general in the Continental Army. Lafayette will become one of General Washington~s most trusted aides.,Answer=19 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00462',',AA.Nen00462,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,yorktown siege;washington;french;general cornwallis;cornwallis,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many thousand men did General Washington have in his siege of Yorktown?,28 September 1781 - General Washington; with a combined Allied army of 17;000 men; begins the siege of Yorktown. French cannons bombard General Cornwallis and his 9000 men day and night while the Allied lines slowly advance and encircle them. British supplies run dangerously low.,Answer=17 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00463',',AA.Nen00463,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,benedict arnold;traitor;american traitor;tarrytown;west point,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many months was Benedict Arnold working for the British before he was discovered as a traitor?,On 23 September 1780 - A British major in civilian clothing is captured near Tarrytown; New York. He is found to be carrying plans indicating Benedict Arnold intends to turn traitor and surrender West Point.  He had been aiding the British since May of 1779.,Answer=17 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00464',',AA.Nen00464,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,yorktown;french;revolutionary war,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The British had 8`700 men at Yorktown.  How many did the combined armies of the Americans and the French have?,At Yorktown; the victory that won the war; Frenchmen outnumbered Americans almost three to one. Washington had 11;000 men engaged in the battle; while the French had at least 29;000 soldiers and sailors. The 37 French ships-of-the-line played a crucial role in trapping the 8700-strong British army and winning the engagement.,Answer=12 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00465',',AA.Nen00465,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,yorktown;washington;french;british,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The French had 29 thousand men at Yorktown.  How many thousand did Washington have?,At Yorktown; the victory that won the war; Frenchmen outnumbered Americans almost three to one. Washington had 11;000 men engaged in the battle; while the French had at least 29;000 soldiers and sailors. The 37 French ships-of-the-line played a crucial role in trapping the 8700-strong British army and winning the engagement.,Answer=11 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00466',',AA.Nen00466,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,boston harbor;tea;tea party;mohawk indians,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Approximately how many thousand pounds sterling was the tea dumped into Boston Harbor worth?,About 50 members of the political organization; The Sons of Liberty; boarded 3 ships in Boston Harbor. Some were dressed; not very convincingly; as Mohawk Indians and dumped 342 crates of tea overboard. In a very orderly and quiet fashion; it was valued at  9;659 pounds sterling.,Answer=10 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00467',',AA.Nen00467,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,general cornwallis;cornwallis;yorktown;general greene;chesapeake bay,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When General Cornwallis arrived in Yorktown` how many thousand men did he have?,On 1 August 1781 - After several months of chasing General Greene~s army without much success; General Cornwallis and his 10;000 tired soldiers arrive to seek rest at the small port of Yorktown; Virginia; on the Chesapeake Bay.,Answer=10 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00468',',AA.Nen00468,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,new york;london;revolutionary war;message,,aPRA1_80 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Approximately how many weeks would it take for a message to travel from New York to London and back during the American Revolution?,,Answer=9 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
