    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00471',',AA.Nen00471,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,son of liberty;boston tea party;revolutionary war;boston harbor;mohawk indians,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Approximately how many ~Sons of Liberty~ took part in the Boston Tea Party?,About 50 members of the political organization; The Sons of Liberty; boarded 3 ships in Boston Harbor. Some were dressed; not very convincingly; as Mohawk Indians and dumped 342 crates of tea overboard. In a very orderly and quiet fashion; it was valued at  9;659 pounds sterling.,Answer=50 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00472',',AA.Nen00472,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,common sense;revolutionary war;king george iii;american independence;thomas paine,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,How many pages did Thomas Paine~s ~Common Sense~ contain?,January 9; 1776 - Thomas Paine~s "Common Sense" is published in Philadelphia. The 50 page pamphlet is highly critical of King George III and attacks allegiance to Monarchy in principle while providing strong arguments for American independence. It becomes an instant best-seller in America. "We have it in our power to begin the world anew...American shall make a stand; not for herself alone; but for the world;" Paine states.,Answer=50 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
