    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00475',',AA.Nen00475,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,yorktown;frenchmen;washington;british,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,Washington had 11 thousand men at Yorktown.  How many thousand did the French have?,At Yorktown; the victory that won the war; Frenchmen outnumbered Americans almost three to one. Washington had 11;000 men engaged in the battle; while the French had at least 29;000 soldiers and sailors. The 37 French ships-of-the-line played a crucial role in trapping the 8700-strong British army and winning the engagement.,Answer=29 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Nen00476',',AA.Nen00476,Ed-U-Games tm,20070604,10,EvWaAm EvPoMi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,quebec;canadian;montgomery,,aPRA1_90 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,The Americans lost 500 men in the Battle of Quebec.  How many did the British and Canadians loose?,On 31st December 1775; with the addition of Montgomery?s troops; Arnold launched night attacks at either end of the city in a snowstorm. The garrison alerted by premature feint attacks on other parts of the city perimeter. Montgomery?s assault was repelled with heavy grapeshot and Montgomery was killed. Arnold?s attack penetrated the city wall but he was wounded. Maclean arrived from dealing with Montgomery?s assault and led the counter attack. The American troops who had penetrated the walls were captured and the assault was driven off. casualties: British and Canadian losses were 20. The American losses were around 500.,Answer=20 LowBracket=0 Type=Integer HiBracket=100,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.NbrLine1KWidth-1.fD.jpg');
